The '''Ongoing Revolutionary Process''' ({{Langx|bl|Processo Revolucionario en Curso}}, '''PREC''') was the period immediately following the [[Baliscan Revolution]], beginning with the [[1919 Confederal Convention]] (starting on 3 October 1919), and continuing until the conclusion of the [[1929 Confederal Convention]], a week before [[W:Black Tuesday|Black Tuesday]] and the advent of the [[W:Great Depression|Great Depression]]. This [[W:Far-left politics|far-left]], [[Anarchism in Balisca|anarchist]]-inspired period was marked by widespread [[W:Anti-clericalism|anti-clericalism]], political turmoil, [[Right-wing insurgency in Balisca|right-wing backlash and insurgencies]], reprisals and counter-reprisals, the [[W:Social ownership#Socialization as a process|socialization]] of companies (and transition to [[W:Cooperative economics|cooperative systems]]), forcible occupation and expropriation of private lands as well as [[W:Economic migrant|talent]] and [[W:Capital flight|capital flight]].

